# A program that asks a question: `run` waits until it writes its prompt,
# and `line` types the answer and waits for a text only the reply holds,
# answering the pane (`%2` on a fresh server), the text, and the line it
# was written on.
# expect: %2 text "letters"
# expect: got 5 letters

opts str ask name 60 10 size
str 'sh -c "printf \"name? \"; read n; echo got \${#n} letters; read n"' command
str 'name? ' wait-text run let ASK
ASK str letters wait-text str fuxth line
ASK kill
